==== Fluid Biomarkers

Paired peripheral and central sampling is the measurement that can separate a retained central state from a continuously driven one (Section @sec:chronic-cns-inflammation).

    - *Plasma, all timepoints*: high-sensitivity CRP, IL-6, soluble IL-6 receptor (sIL-6R), gp130, CHI3L1/YKL-40
    - *CSF, baseline and 12 months*: sTREM2, CHI3L1/YKL-40, IL-6 and sIL-6R, in participants who consent to lumbar puncture
    - *Paired analysis*: peripheral and central markers sampled within 7 days of each PET scan
    - *Persistence rule*: a participant counts as "peripheral-normalised" when hs-CRP and IL-6 return to the reference range; the primary persistence analysis tests whether TSPO binding remains elevated in that group

No ME/CFS study has reported CHI3L1/YKL-40 or IL-6 trans-signalling. These measures are exploratory and discovery-oriented, not validation of an established marker.
